<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Stucco repair in Airdrie and Chestermere starts the way it does in Calgary: someone looks at the wall and tells you what is actually wrong. This page puts homeowners in both cities in touch with independent stucco contractors, who quote and contract directly with you. Airdrie had 74,100 residents in the 2021 census, up 20.3% from 2016, and Chestermere had 22,163, up 11.4%.</p><p>This site is an advertisement paid by contractors. It does no stucco work itself and holds no trade licence, insurance or warranty, so credentials, warranty terms and price are between you and the contractor who quotes your wall. Coverage includes Airdrie, Chestermere and Calgary. Call <strong>(403) 555-0148</strong> or email <strong>info@sandstonestucco.ca</strong>.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Airdrie & Chestermere</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Airdrie & Chestermere Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Crack and patch repair</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Hairline cracks, chips and gaps around windows and doors, quoted by an independent contractor after seeing the wall. Ask them to open any soft or bubbling area before pricing it.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Hail damage scope</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A written repair estimate you can pass to your insurer after a hailstorm. IBC names Airdrie among the areas the June 2020 storm hit; a contractor can tell you whether marks on your wall are storm damage.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Woodpecker hole repair</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Northern flicker holes patched once nesting is over and the hole is empty. Ask the contractor how they close the hole and, on an EIFS wall, how they reinforce the foam behind the finish.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Foundation parging recoat</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A fresh parging coat where the finish over the foundation wall is cracking or flaking. This is a surface recoat only, not foundation crack repair or waterproofing.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
